    {
      "id": "17848",
      "key": "SFCC-22",
      "summary": "SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing",
      "description": "Epic Summary\n\n\nThis epic instruments the SFCC PWA Kit to support Zimmermann's full analytics, tagging, consent, and experimentation requirements across all regional storefronts. It covers loading the GTM container, building a well-structured data layer as the single source of truth for all downstream analytics and marketing tags, integrating Didomi for consent management and Google Consent Mode v2, and embedding Optimizely and Crazy Egg scripts directly on the PWA. The outcome is a clean, compliant, and fully observable storefront that gives Zimmermann's analytics and marketing teams the data foundation they need from day one.\nBusiness Value / Objective\n\n\nZimmermann's current Magento platform has fragmented analytics instrumentation, contributing to incomplete data flows and unreliable tracking. Re-platforming to SFCC is an opportunity to establish a robust, structured data layer from the ground up — ensuring all commerce events (page views, product impressions, add-to-cart, checkout steps, purchase) are consistently captured across all 8 storefronts and routed correctly through GTM and AddingWell to GA4 and downstream marketing platforms. Accurate data is critical for conversion rate optimisation, A/B testing, and Zimmermann's broader data and analytics strategy.\nScope\nIn Scope\nGTM container snippet loaded on all storefront pages across all 8 regional sites via the AddingWell MRT integration (AAB-001)\nData layer build: well-structured, commerce-native data layer covering all key customer and product interactions across the full shopping journey — page views, product impressions, add-to-cart, checkout steps, purchase, and other required events (AAB-002); Tell No Lies data dictionary used as reference\nConsistent data layer population regardless of consent state — consent gating of advertising/personalisation tags is handled downstream by Didomi, Sparro, and AddingWell (AAB-003)\nDidomi SDK load in PWA Kit: SDK loaded on all storefront pages, consent API exposed to PWA components, Google Consent Mode v2 integration (SFCC-107)\nOptimizely script loaded directly in PWA page head (US storefront only) to initialise before render and avoid test flicker (AAB-004)\nCrazy Egg script loaded directly in PWA page head across all storefronts for session recording and heatmap capture from page load (AAB-005)\nOut of Scope\nGTM container logic, tag configuration, and AddingWell container setup — owned by Zimmermann/Tell No Lies\nGA4 configuration and tag setup — owned by Zimmermann\nDidomi console configuration: vendor IDs, purpose IDs, cookie categories, regional defaults, banner UI — owned by Zimmermann\nOptimizely audience configuration and experiment setup — owned by Zimmermann via GTM/AddingWell\nCrazy Egg script configuration, consent gating, session recording suppression, and PII masking — owned by Zimmermann\nSEO build: URL strategy, canonical tags, hreflang, XML sitemaps, robots.txt, structured data schema, meta tags, and 301 redirects — all covered in SFCC-20 Data Migration (DMU-013–DMU-042)\nInside Chat widget loading — loaded via GTM script injection through AddingWell (Zimmermann scope)\nDependencies\nSFCC-1 Platform Setup & Environments — PWA Kit foundation must be in place before GTM and analytics instrumentation can begin\nSFCC-2 PWA Kit Components — data layer events are tied to component interactions; component builds across other epics must expose the correct hooks\nTell No Lies (Zimmermann's analytics partner) — Tell No Lies data dictionary and event specification must be finalised and signed off before data layer build begins\nDidomi — SDK version and consent API spec must be confirmed before SFCC-107 can be completed\nAddingWell — MRT integration approach must be confirmed for GTM container loading\nAssumptions & Constraints\nThe Tell No Lies data dictionary is the authoritative reference for all data layer event names and payload structure; Accenture will build to this spec once signed off\nAll GTM container logic, tag routing, and AddingWell configuration are outside Accenture scope — SFCC delivers the data layer and script loading only\nOptimizely is scoped to the US storefront only at launch (AAB-004)\nCrazy Egg script configuration including PII masking and consent gating is owned by Zimmermann; SFCC scope is script loading only (AAB-005)\nDidomi Accenture scope is SDK loading and Google Consent Mode v2 integration only — all Didomi platform configuration remains with Zimmermann\nPriority:\n Medium\nTarget Release / Sprint:\n Sprint 7",
